# text = And now I desire that this inequality should be no more in this land, especially among this my people; but I desire that this land be a land of liberty, and every man may enjoy his rights and privileges alike, so long as the Lord sees fit that we may live and inherit the land, yea, even as long as any of our posterity remains upon the face of the land.
# sent_id = 926
# llm_note = Two "I desire that" ccomp clauses, contrasted by "but". First desire: "that this inequality should be no more". Second desire: "that this land be a land of liberty, and every man may enjoy..." — "be" is subjunctive cop. "so long as the Lord sees fit that we may live and inherit" = advcl of "enjoy"/"remain". "yea, even as long as any of our posterity remains" = conj advcl. "this my people" — "this" is det, "my" is nmod:poss inside the NP.
