# text = And they did wax strong in love towards Mosiah; yea, they did esteem him more than any other man; for they did not look upon him as a tyrant who was seeking for gain, yea, for that lucre which doth corrupt the soul; for he had not exacted riches of them, neither had he delighted in the shedding of blood; but he had established peace in the land, and he had granted unto his people that they should be delivered from all manner of bondage; therefore they did esteem him, yea, exceedingly, beyond measure.
# sent_id = 933
# llm_note = Long sentence with many conj clauses. Root = "wax" (token 4, emphatic "did wax"). "strong" = xcomp of "wax". "yea, they did esteem" = conj. "for they did not look upon him as a tyrant" = advcl (causal). "who was seeking for gain" = acl:relcl on "tyrant". "yea, for that lucre which doth corrupt the soul" = appositive NP ("lucre" in appos to "gain"). "for he had not exacted" = conj advcl. "neither had he delighted" — "neither" ADV, inverted, conj. "but he had established peace...and he had granted" = conj clauses. "that they should be delivered" = ccomp of "granted". "therefore they did esteem him" = final conj. "yea, exceedingly, beyond measure" = adverbial elaboration.
